%I A401395 #12 Oct 31 2026 16:26:37
%S A401395 1,4,22,283,4717,108992,8925672
%N A401395 The number of semirings with zero of size n up to isomorphism.
%C A401395 A semiring is a set S with two binary operations + and * such that (S, +) is a commutative semigroup, and (S, *) is a semigroup, and multiplication distributes over addition. A semiring with zero requires (S, +) to have an identity 0, such that 0 * x = x * 0 = 0 for all x in S.
%H A401395 J. Edwards, J. D. Mitchell, and P. Ragavan, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.03709">Counting finite semirings</a>, arXiv:2507.03709 [math.RA], 2025-2026. See Table 1.
%F A401395 Since all semirings with zero are semirings, a(n) <= A401124(n).
%Y A401395 Cf. A000001, A001423, A027623, A027851, A305858, A401124.
%K A401395 nonn,more,hard,new
%O A401395 1,2
